        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts the Woodville Historical Society, founded in 1976, which preserves artifacts and hosts events like the annual Tomato Festival celebrating its tomato‑growing past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/24677",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Woodville’s public library is a branch of the Birchard Public Library of Sandusky County, offering residents access to regional collections.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former Pennsylvania Railroad crossed the Portage River in Woodville, marking the town’s role in early rail transport.",
